# WARNING: the existence of this file makes npm ignore .gitignore completely.
# Anything excluded there must be excluded here too, or it ships. This file
# used to have four lines, and `npm pack` was carrying 821 JPEG frames of a
# screen recording, the .work recon of a real product, and three licensed MP3s.

# --- Never publish: other people's licensed assets -------------------------
# Stock-music licences cover using a track in a video, not redistributing the
# file. A published package hands the raw audio to everyone who installs it.
# The music *mechanism* ships; the music does not. See
# template/public/audio/music/README.md.
# Music ships — the owner confirmed redistribution rights.

# --- Never publish: secrets ------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Never publish: one run's output against somebody's product ------------
# Screen recordings are hundreds of JPEGs (~140MB), and .work holds recon of a
# real site plus the judge's notes. Both are outputs of using the tool, not
# part of it.
**/.work/**
**/runs/**
**/public/assets/**
!**/public/assets/.gitkeep
**/audio/*.wav
**/audio/audio.json
**/audio/vo/**

# --- Never publish: render artefacts ---------------------------------------
**/out/**
**/output*.mp4

# --- Never publish: build and local junk -----------------------------------
**/node_modules/**
*.log
*.docx
*.zip
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Reference frames extracted from other companies' launch films. The written
# analysis in skills/pitchframe-motion-language ships; the footage never does.
**/frameybyframe/**
